Table~\ref{tab:sensitivity_b1} reports Task~B1 classification metrics across six NVE thresholds. Task~B1 achieves $\text{AUROC} = 1.000$ because the minimum positive NVE ($4.02\times$, exp~008e\_v3\_s3) exceeds the maximum negative NVE ($3.78\times$, exp~008e\_v3\_s2), yielding perfect rank separation. The optimal threshold lies in the interval $(3.78, 4.02]$; we report $\geq 3.9\times$ as a representative value. Table~\ref{tab:sensitivity_b2} provides the corresponding analysis for Task~B2 ($\text{AUROC} = 0.958$, imperfect separation due to 008e\_v3\_s2).

